    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102081" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶρυ</span></b> , τό, a kind of
		ore, perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ferrous sulphate,
				melanterite</i>: nom. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶρι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					5.102
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶρυ</span> as cited by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
			</span></i>); the gen. is <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώρεως</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hippiatr.</u>
				70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				96
			</span></i>; <i>soreos</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				6.9.5
			</span></i>; <i>soreos</i> (v.l.
			<i>sorios, soryos</i>) in <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				34.117
			</span></i>.</div>
